! Grammar-first progression

A ''map of concepts'', not a rigid calendar. A learner can navigate forward or backward as needed.

!! Stage 0: phonological and writing foundations
* [[Grammar/Tones and Pinyin]] — tone categories and the third-tone sandhi pattern
* [[Character/Character Structure]] — semantic/phonetic components and radical indexing

!! Stage 1: elementary clause architecture
* [[Grammar/SVO Word Order]] — basic predicate–argument structure
* [[Grammar/Negation with 不 and 没]] — contrasting negators
* [[Grammar/Questions with 吗]] — polar questions
* [[Grammar/Classifiers]] — number/demonstrative + classifier + noun

!! Stage 2: organizing information and events
* [[Grammar/Topic and Comment]] — topicalization
* [[Grammar/Aspect and Tense]] — reference time vs viewpoint
* [[Grammar/Perfective 了]] — perfective viewpoint, not a past tense
* [[Grammar/Progressive 在]] — action in progress

!! Stage 3 (planned, not yet authored)
Resultative complements, directional complements, `把` and `被`, comparisons, modal verbs, relative clauses, discourse particles, and increasingly advanced narrative grammar.

